      "sequence_position": 13,
      "problem": "$\\,$ If $x>2,$ then ${x}^{3}>3.$\n\nWhich of the following is logically equivalent to the conditional predicate above?",
      "worked_solution": "Let's denote by $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x>2.$\n\n- $Q(x):$ ${x}^{3}>3.$\n\nThen, our initial sentence can be written as $P(x)⇒Q(x),$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n¬P(x)∨Q(x).\n$$\n\nThe negation of $P(x)$ can be written as\n\n- $¬P(x):$ $x\\le 2.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x\\le 2,$ or ${x}^{3}>3.$",
